      {
        "id": "z4tbkzCdb55abwak",
        "title": "Welcome to CLUE",
        "content": {
          "type": "Text",
          "format": "html",
          "text": [
            "<h2>Welcome to CLUE!</h2><p>CLUE is a platform that helps your class figure things out together as a community of scientists and engineers. On clue you can work individually and in a group, and you can share your ideas with the class and see other people&#x27;s ideas.</p><p>In CLUE, everyone works in a group. When you start an activity, you can choose a group. You can change groups by clicking on the group number in the upper right corner. Then, you can either join an existing group or start a new group.</p><p><strong>Right now, make sure you are in the same group as the other students you are sitting and working with. If your groupmates need help, help them! You&#x27;re figuring things out together.</strong></p>"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "QyZF84K3NWyhup6f",
        "title": "Lesson Structure in the Lessons and Resources Pane",
        "content": {
          "type": "Text",
          "format": "html",
          "text": [
            "<p>Each lesson in CLUE has four parts. The orange tabs above show each part.</p><p>You&#x27;re engineering a new device, and the parts can help you organize your thinking.</p><ul><li><span data-slate-type=\"highlight\" data-slate-highlight-id=\"2defbc3d-d690-4d7a-9ea4-196cd86bfbf3\"></span>: That&#x27;s where you are now! This is where you&#x27;ll start thinking about a new problem and figuring out the science behind it.</li></ul><p>The other three are:</p><ul><li>Design</li><li>Develop</li><li>Evaluate</li></ul><p>You&#x27;ll learn more about these when you get there.</p><p>When you&#x27;re done with one part, go to the next one.</p>"
          ],
          "highlightedText": [
            {
              "id": "2defbc3d-d690-4d7a-9ea4-196cd86bfbf3",
              "text": "Investigate"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
