      {
        "id": "kW-ECMZPRj_YT6mZ",
        "title": "Thinking about your hand...",
        "content": {
          "type": "Text",
          "format": "html",
          "text": [
            "<p>Okay, you know the basics! Let&#x27;s jump into figuring things out!</p><p></p><p>Biological hands can do a LOT of things! Plus, your brain and muscles are already &quot;wired&quot; to work well with a hand.</p><p>Even though we might not make something that looks or works exactly the same, understanding how hands work can give us good ideas about how to design prostheses.</p>"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "nIRx2puiKA2M6EOx",
        "title": "With your group!",
        "content": {
          "type": "Question",
          "version": 1,
          "locked": false,
          "questionId": "LS3asG",
          "tiles": [
            {
              "id": "Q1aE3371i7kjY7BT",
              "title": "Thinking about your hand...",
              "fixedPosition": true,
              "content": {
                "type": "Text",
                "format": "html",
                "text": [
                  "<p>With your group, find three different ways you can to move an object.</p><p>For each way you find, write down what motion or motions are you making with your hand?</p>"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "I-QSLZ-XcsTqZS9H",
              "title": "Recording your ideas.",
              "content": {
                "type": "Text",
                "format": "html",
                "text": [
                  "<p>When you drag the blue question tile over, you&#x27;ll be able to write here.</p><p>If you want, you can also add a table, take a picture of what you draw, or sketch something.</p>"
