      {
        "id": "_croJICfTtypkjTD",
        "title": "Class Discussion - Placeholder",
        "content": {
          "type": "Text",
          "format": "html",
          "text": [
            "<p><span data-slate-type=\"highlight\" data-slate-highlight-id=\"5b7e6d05-83a9-4f47-8c15-3893dc630df9\"></span></p><p>Also, start making a class-wide simple box &amp; arrow model/flowchart:</p><p>muscles --&gt; tendons --&gt; movement</p>"
          ],
          "highlightedText": [
            {
              "id": "5b7e6d05-83a9-4f47-8c15-3893dc630df9",
              "text": "Also possibly note that students get some \"points\" for coming up with different motions.Also possibly add in the biomimicry stuff."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "zyoT6wp_c7IxjDmS",
        "title": "How do hands even work?",
        "content": {
          "type": "Text",
          "format": "html",
          "text": [
            "<p>Researchers from the University of Southern California and MIT used images from medical scans to make simulations of the hand.</p><p></p><p>Add video and write-up, as well as an image of the nerves.</p>"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "nuWVwz755ToqhQYm",
        "title": "What makes the motion happen?",
        "content": {
          "type": "Text",
          "format": "html",
          "text": [
            "<p>Go back to where you wrote down the motions you make and draw or write what tendons, muscles, or other parts of your hand you think you use to make that motion.</p>"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "hvOHWCAjeuaWttC3",
        "title": "Moving on...",
